  "lead": "Adjusted gross income on individual returns was <b>$14.78 trillion</b> in tax year 2022, from <b>159,651,330</b> returns (SRC-621-01). Massachusetts AGI was <b>$422.21 billion</b> on 3,567,790 returns, rank 9 of 51 (derived, SRC-621-01). Among Massachusetts counties, <b>Middlesex County</b> had the most adjusted gross income in tax year 2022 at <b>$125.60 billion</b> (derived, SRC-621-02). Among Florida counties, <b>Miami-Dade County</b> had the most AGI at <b>$160.81 billion</b> (derived, SRC-621-02). A dedicated AGI-percentile-by-state file is not posted; size-of-AGI stubs are stored under derived.secondary. Returns with $1 million or more of AGI held <b>21.87%</b> of Massachusetts AGI in tax year 2022, from <b>27,270</b> returns (SRC-621-03). Returns with $200,000 or more held <b>54.62%</b> of AGI (SRC-621-03). Massachusetts ranks 7 of 51 on the million-plus AGI share (derived, SRC-621-03). A dedicated percentile-by-state file is not posted.",
